<!-- FAQ -->
<section id="faq">
  <div class="section-label" data-r>Common questions</div>
  <h2 class="range-headline" data-r data-delay="1">
    Everything<br>
    you need to know.
  </h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q">Is Deep Sleep habit-forming?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">
        <div class="faq-a-inner">
          No, and this matters more than people realise. Deep Sleep is built around botanicals like Valerian Root, Lemon
          Balm, and Passionflower, which support your body&rsquo;s own relaxation pathways rather than forcing sedation.
          They&rsquo;re non-addictive by nature. The 5mg melatonin works with your circadian rhythm, not against it, so
          your body never becomes dependent on it to produce its own melatonin. You can take Deep Sleep every night or
          just when you need it. Either way, stopping is effortless.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q">Will it make me groggy the next morning?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">
        <div class="faq-a-inner">
          No. This is something we thought hard about. Many sleep supplements use 5&ndash;10mg of melatonin, which
          floods your system and lingers into the morning, that&rsquo;s what causes the foggy head. Deep Sleep uses a
          precise 5mg dose, calibrated for overnight effectiveness without the hangover. The botanical ingredients are
          lipid-soluble and metabolise efficiently, so by the time your alarm goes off, your body has processed them
          cleanly. You wake up rested, not sedated.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q">When will I feel results?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">
        <div class="faq-a-inner">
          Most people notice something on the first night: a gentler wind-down, less time staring at the ceiling.
          Because it&rsquo;s a liquid shot, the ingredients absorb significantly faster than capsules or gummies, which
          have to dissolve before your body can use them. For the deeper benefits (staying asleep longer, waking up more
          restored), most users report a clear shift within 3 to 5 nights as the botanical compounds build consistency
          in your system. Take it 20&ndash;30 minutes before bed for the best results.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q">What does it taste like?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">
        <div class="faq-a-inner">
          Tropical Peach &amp; Mango: light, clean, and genuinely refreshing. We spent time getting this right because
          the last thing you want before bed is something that tastes like medicine or leaves an aftertaste. There are
          zero artificial sweeteners, zero sugar, and no chemical finish. Just a small shot you&rsquo;ll actually look
          forward to. It doubles as a nice pre-sleep ritual too: a quiet moment that signals to your body: it&rsquo;s
          time to wind down.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q">Is it safe to take with medication?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">
        <div class="faq-a-inner">
          If you&rsquo;re on prescribed medication, please check with your doctor or pharmacist before adding any
          supplement, and that applies to Deep Sleep as it would to anything else. Melatonin can interact with certain
          medications including blood thinners, immunosuppressants, and some antidepressants. The botanical ingredients
          (Valerian Root, Ashwagandha, Passionflower, and others) are generally well-tolerated, but individual
          circumstances vary. When in doubt, a quick conversation with your healthcare provider takes two minutes and
          gives you complete clarity.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-q">Is it vegan and allergen-free?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
      <div class="faq-a">
        <div class="faq-a-inner">
          Yes, fully. Deep Sleep is 100% vegan, non-GMO, gluten-free, and dairy-free. We use no artificial colours, no
          artificial preservatives, and no fillers. Every ingredient is either a plant extract or a mineral (Magnesium
          Glycinate), and the formula is manufactured to GMP standards. If you have specific allergen concerns, the full
          ingredient list is available on the label and we&rsquo;re happy to answer any questions directly.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

